            <ArticleTitle>Coronary fistula from left main stem to main pulmonary artery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>600-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a patient with a rare coronary arteriovenous fistula connecting the left main stem to the main pulmonary artery. This rare case was discovered during routine coronary angiography for the evaluation of the patient s coronary heart disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
